      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. Year 1266 in the Discordian calendar corresponds to ISO year 100 (1266 - 1166 = 100), which is divisible by 100 but not 400, so it's not a leap year. I'll improve understandability with a descriptive test name, better variable names, and clarifying context.Let me check the working directory and find the expected file location.The script expects the file in the current working directory. I need to write the file directly there.The test compiled successfully. The improved test replaces the generic `test15()` method name with `test_isLeapYear_returnsFalse_forCenturyYearNotDivisibleBy400()`, adds a comment explaining why year 1266 is not a leap year (it maps to ISO year 100, a century year not divisible by 400), and uses descriptive variable names — all while preserving the identical runtime behaviour."
